course: dictionary
lesson: 11548
title: Amiable: friendly and easy to like
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a person's character, the way they behave and feel. Amiable is one of these. When you meet it, look at what the person does and says around it. «The amiable neighbour waved and brought us some apples.» A neighbour who waves and shares apples is friendly, so amiable means friendly and easy to like.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense. «Our amiable teacher always greets us with a smile.» Does «Our friendly teacher always greets us with a smile» still make sense? Yes, so friendly is a good meaning for amiable.
explain: Amiable often describes a mood or a chat too. «Dad was in an amiable mood, so he let us stay up late.» The mood was pleasant, so Dad was happy to be easy-going. An amiable chat is a pleasant, friendly talk.
fact: Amiable means friendly, pleasant and easy to like.
fact: Amiable is an adjective: amiable, more amiable, most amiable.
fact: Amiable is used for people, animals and moods: «an amiable person», «an amiable dog», «amiable mood».
fact: Clues for amiable: smiling, waving, sharing, or being cheerful and kind.
fact: The opposite of amiable is unfriendly, so an amiable person is never rude or cross.
exercise: «The amiable neighbour waved and brought us some apples.» What does amiable mean? | Angry and grumpy | *Friendly and easy to like | Very tall | Lost and confused
exercise: What in this sentence is a clue to amiable? «The amiable new girl smiled and shared her crayons.» | The word new | *Shared her crayons and smiled | The word girl | The name Mia
exercise: Which word could replace amiable in «The amiable dog wagged its tail at every visitor»? | *Friendly | Muddy | Cross | Sleepy
test: «Our amiable teacher always greets us with a smile.» Which word is closest in meaning to amiable? | *Friendly | Strict | Lazy | Noisy
test: «Dad was in an amiable mood, so he let us stay up late.» What does amiable mood mean? | A mood for running | A cross, grumpy mood | *A friendly, pleasant mood | A sleepy mood
exam: «The amiable shopkeeper chatted with every customer and said goodbye with a wave.» What does amiable mean? | Very quiet | Rude and unfriendly | *Pleasant and easy to like | Very quick
